   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reporting an order",
     "texto": [
      "When you report what someone told you to do, the command turns into **que + imperfect subjunctive**:\n\n- «**Llámame**.» → Me dijo que lo **llamara**.\n- «**No vengas**.» → Me pidió que no **viniera**.\n- «**Entregue** el informe.» → Me ordenó que **entregara** el informe.\n\nThe verb in the main clause tells what type of command it was: **pidió**, **aconsejó**, **rogó**, **prohibió**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Information or order",
     "texto": [
      "The **mood** of the second verb tells what is being reported:\n\n- Information → **indicative**: Me dijo que **venía**. (he was coming)\n- Order or request → **subjunctive**: Me dijo que **viniera**. (I was to come)\n\nIf the main verb is in the present, the present subjunctive is enough: **Dice** que lo **llames**.\n\nWhen reporting, words of time and place also change:\n\n- hoy → **aquel día**; mañana → **al día siguiente**\n- aquí → **allí**; este → **ese** or **aquel**\n- venir → **ir**; traer → **llevar**"
     ],
